WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
I'm in Tromsø, in Norway, in the Arctic Circle,

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.360
And this beautiful thing here;

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.080
is one of the boats that plies the Hurtigruten,

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.220
and I am probably mispronouncing that.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.600
But the fast route from
down in the south-west of Norway,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.140
all the way to here in the Arctic Circle.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.560
And I say fast route, it takes seven days.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.020
But here is something you might not know,

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.260
this is an excellent example of slow television.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:27.440
Something that the NRK, the National Broadcaster,

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.300
the equivalent of the BBC or PBS, excels at.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.260
In 2011 they took a load of cameras and just attached them

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.200
to this boat and broadcast its journey 24 hours a day

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.140
as it went up. Well not specifically this boat,

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.660
one very much like it.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:44.480
Also, because they did it in the middle of summer and it was not

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.140
a freezing cold mid-afternoon -

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.280
-- it's about 2:30 as I record this --

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.840
It was beautiful all the way.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.800
Norwegan fjords, gorgeous sun, well if you want to see it

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.240
fortunately they released all the footage through Creative Commons,

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.820
so there's some interesting mashups here on YouTube

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.400
if you don't want to wait the full 134 hours.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.700
But people did. Here's the strange thing: people did watch this.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.700
Maybe just for a few minutes, maybe for a few hours,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.440
maybe they just kept it on the television all the time,

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:14.260
in the same way as they kept on the train that stayed for 24 hours

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.100
thorough Norway or the log fire

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:20.760
that simply burned. Slow television is an antidote to the

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:24.760
reality TV show and the fast cut editing of today.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.820
And is it massively popular?

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.300
Well, no, of course not, that's why you're watching

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.420
2 minute videos on YouTube rather than 134 hours

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.980
of footage of a boat, but

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.800
don't rule it out because its surprising how many people will just tune in for a little while,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.060
to something calming and pleasant and slow

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.460
And that is something you might not have known.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.720
